      "task_id": "T6",
      "title": "Baseline fraud model",
      "objective": "Train a baseline classifier for the synthetic fraud label on the medical claims: logistic regression plus one tree-based model. Hold out a quarter of the claims with a split that preserves the class balance in both partitions, using the run seed, and report the positive-class prevalence in each partition. Use only features that would be legitimately available at prediction time: exclude identifiers and any field that is derived from the label. Fit every preprocessing step (encoding, scaling) on the training partition only. Report precision, recall, F1, PR-AUC, ROC-AUC and the confusion matrix for each model on the held-out partition, save the final feature list, and state the limitations: synthetic label, class imbalance, a baseline model, and no operational use.",
      "tags": [
        "modeling",
        "fraud",
        "classification",
        "leakage",
        "splits",
        "seeds",
        "metrics",
        "class_imbalance"
      ],
